# A hosted Foundation's settings (docs/hosting.md). Copy to deploy/.env (never committed) and fill in.

# The name people open, without https://. DNS for it points at this machine (or at the tunnel).
# The server's public address is https://<this>, and Google's redirect is https://<this>/auth/google/callback
FOUNDATION_DOMAIN=foundation.example.com

# Who may sign in: emails or @domains of the company's Google accounts. Nobody else gets a session.
FOUNDATION_ALLOWLIST=@example.com
# Who arrives as an admin (everyone else arrives as a member; an admin can change a role afterwards)
FOUNDATION_ADMIN_EMAILS=you@example.com

# Foundation's own Google client (Google Cloud console → APIs & Services → Credentials → OAuth client ID,
# type Web application; consent screen Internal, so only the company's Workspace accounts can use it).
# Authorized redirect URI: https://<FOUNDATION_DOMAIN>/auth/google/callback
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Optional. A token other services and agents use for /mcp and /api (32+ characters)
# FOUNDATION_SERVICE_TOKEN=
# Optional. Agent turns on a hosted server run on API credits (there is no signed-in Claude Code on it)
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Optional. Huddles connect people's browsers directly; across strict networks they need a TURN server
# FOUNDATION_ICE_SERVERS=[{"urls":"turn:turn.example.com:3478","username":"…","credential":"…"}]
# Optional. Make everyone take a desktop release the server can't work without (after it is published)
# FOUNDATION_MIN_CLIENT=

# How many nightly database copies the backup keeps (the file archive is never pruned)
# FOUNDATION_BACKUP_KEEP=14
# Only with `--profile tunnel`: the Cloudflare Tunnel's token (no ports 80/443 opened on this machine)
# CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN=

# Never set FOUNDATION_DEV_LOGIN on a hosted server.
